  "frontier_coordinate": "R-156 remains the direct A13 frontier. Its intrinsic normalized shifted-state gap has the exact sufficient radius criterion L_*(R) r sqrt(1+r^2/16)+2 U_* sqrt(2(1-(1+r^2)^(-1/2)))<47/1000, but the pinned finite cylinder, upper operator norm U_*, and third-variation modulus L_*(R) are not registered, so no numerical or cutoff-uniform radius follows. No intrinsic counterexample was certified. In the phase-neutral side branch, R-157 proves that the hash-pinned unconstrained M1/P1 functional has zero as its unique critical point and global minimizer and forces exponential decay. R-158 separately solves PA-M1-Q: an imposed fixed charge or grand potential produces exact finite-shell first-order coexistence, but the state remains above the original neutral zero reference, its registered local observables are uniform, and no physical charge or reservoir is derived. PA-M1-Q is therefore a conditional mechanism, not a physical-vacuum selection. T-054 next compares the structurally distinct PA-M5-NL3-SV candidate. T-050, A13, Nelson, and Sector-A closure remain open.",
